{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: cut the per-act cost of appending a merge's succession.\n\nhugh asked on 2026-10-16 why landing in the artroom workroom still takes so long, and approved filing this.\n\nIn the real artroom landing on 2026-10-16 (receipt at 09:36:30), the resident appended 58 successor artifacts at about 2.8 s each and 104 retirements at about 0.8 s each, from commit times in the log: about 4.5 minutes after the receipt. Every landing pays this, in proportion to the paths it changes. The candidate design notes/2026-09-02-durable-append-batching.md (branch request/append-batching-design, not merged, no implementation authorized) measured the Git process count of one append but not where the 0.8–2.8 s goes.\n\nOutcome. First measure where one succession append spends its time at this depth: Git processes, fold append, staleness, signing or HTTP. Then remove the dominant cost, so a succession of N acts costs much less than N separate full appends. The signed intent, the sequencer signature, admission and the compare-and-swap of the sequence ref keep their guarantees. If the fix needs a protocol change, such as one sequenced batch, first publish a design note for review, refreshed from the September note, and say so in the report.","body":{"conditions":"1. The report states the measured per-act append time of successor artifacts and retirements on a frozen artroom copy, before and after, and the profile showing where it went. 2. The 58-successor, 104-retirement succession of the artroom replay appends in under one minute, or the report says plainly what the measured floor is and why. 3. Each appended act remains individually signed, admitted and sequenced as today, or a reviewed design note authorizes otherwise before implementation. 4. Projections at the same frontier are byte-identical before and after on a frozen copy. 5. go test ./... passes at the head.","target_head":"5876d2118fa3d9d223dfc923744bc0bb9ef1dfc0","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}